{pad:ignore}
<p><code>{fake:rows}</code> makes values that look real enough for a prototype, a designer's
preview or a demo page - a person's name, an address at example.org, a price, a date, an
IBAN that passes the check of a bank that is not there - from the seeded sequence the
<code>padFake*</code> helpers of seeders use. A kind is a file of <code>pad/subs/fakes/types/</code>,
a few lines that answer the value and read their options; a kind is added by adding its
file.</p>

<p>One kind is the tag's value. Several kinds, <code>rows=</code> or a pair make rows: the
level's data, iterated by the content or kept by <code>toData=</code>, each field under its
kind's name - or as <code>'customer:name'</code> names it. An email or a username in a row
with a name is that person's, a slug in a row with a title that title's. A FALSE of <code>boolean</code> is a miss, so the
<code>@else@</code> shows.</p>

<p>The values are the same on every request: the <code>{fake:rows}</code> tags of a request share
a sequence started from one seed, and <code>seed=</code> gives a tag values of its own - the
rows <code>padFakeRows ( 'name, email', 5, 7 )</code> gives in PHP. The page's own sequence,
its <code>padFakeSeed</code>, is left where it was. The kinds are never reached bare - their
names are the names of fields - only as the fake type, <code>{fake:email/}</code>.</p>
{/pad:ignore}
